      "description": "Watch Gimnasia LP vs Atletico Tucuman highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina action returned on August 17, 2026 , as Gimnasia LP hosted Atletico Tucuman in a fixture that promised intensity and tactical intrigue. Both sides looked to assert dominance early on, creating a charged atmosphere that would eventually dictate the course of the evening. Early Tension and a Crucial Dismissal The match began with a flurry of physical challenges, as the referee was forced to reach for his pocket early. Ignacio Miramon was the first to see yellow in the 23rd minute, followed quickly by Tiago Palacios and Gaston Benedetti . The game's complexion changed dramatically in the 35th minute when Alexis Steimbach was shown a straight red card. Amidst heavy protests from his teammates, the dismissal left Atletico Tucuman shorthanded and struggling to contain the mounting pressure. Gimnasia LP capitalized just before the break, as Eros Mancuso found the back of the net in the 43rd minute after a precise assist from Joaquin Tobio Burgos , sending the home side into the interval with a narrow lead. Second Half Surge and Red Card Woes The restart didn't bring any relief for the visitors. In the 50th minute, German Conti received a yellow card, and just three minutes later, he was shown a second yellow, resulting in another red card. Now facing a massive numerical disadvantage, Atletico Tucuman found it impossible to stem the tide. Tiago Palacios doubled the lead in the 60th minute, finishing off a move orchestrated by Adolfo Gaich . The tactical shift saw Guido Carrillo and Joaquin Correa enter the fray, with the latter providing the assist for Joaquin Tobio Burgos to score the third goal in the 70th minute. Closing the Show As the clock ticked down, Gimnasia LP remained relentless. Eric Meza , who came on as a substitute, provided the assist for Alexis Castro to hammer home the fourth goal in the 84th minute. Despite a late yellow card for Manuel Panaro , the result was never in doubt. The final whistle confirmed a comprehensive performance from the hosts, who took full advantage of their opponents' disciplinary struggles on a memorable night of football."
